  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "5.0.0 — the first release intended for use. .NET client for the ECM (AppGateway) APIs: documents and their versions, files, tags and tag management, per-document ACL, lookups, tagging-rule sync and the outbox event feed, over the client-credentials + on-behalf token exchange, so every call is ACL-trimmed to the acting user. Where documents land is decided by the credential: an ECM administrator grants an integration client one workspace, that grant travels in the token, and nothing on the client side names a workspace — an application writing to several declares one credential per workspace under Ecm:Connections, each resolved as a keyed IEcmClient. The retired configuration keys (Ecm:ClientCredentials:*, Ecm:DefaultWorkspace, Ecm:DefaultWorkspaceId, Ecm:WorkspaceMode, Ecm:ValidateWorkspaceOnStartup) are refused at startup with the replacement named rather than ignored silently, and startup logs which workspace each credential writes to. services.AddHealthChecks().AddEcm() reports whether the integration is configured well enough to work, including a membership revoked after the token was minted; DocumentUploadRequest.IdempotencyKey makes a repeated upload safe; Ecm:Documents:IncludeTags / :IncludeMetadata set what a document list carries for the calls that do not say, and Ecm:TagManagement:IncludeAllNamespaces does the same for the admin taxonomy listings, so an integration that never reads tags — or one whose job is the taxonomy screens — configures it once instead of at every call site. Multi-targets net8.0 and net10.0, with the shared contracts assembly bundled inside the package. Requires an ECM server from this release. See CHANGELOG.md, shipped in this package.",
